# apex patch: persona hardware decode => mediaCapabilities powerEfficient=true
#
# THE PROBLEM. navigator.mediaCapabilities.decodingInfo({h264 1080p}) reports
# {supported: true, smooth: true, powerEfficient: false} in the container --
# powerEfficient comes from MediaCapabilities::GetGpuFactoriesSupport, which
# asks the renderer's GPU factories; without a GPU process it calls
# OnGpuFactoriesSupport(false) for every query. A real GPU desktop reports
# powerEfficient=true for h264 1080p. Fingerprinters score exactly this
# GPU-truth vs persona mismatch (and cross-check it against WebCodecs hw
# flags -- the two must agree).
#
# THE FIX. In GetGpuFactoriesSupport, when the persona claims hardware decode
# (APEX_FP_MEDIA_HW_DECODE=1), answer the GPU factories query with
# supported=true and return -- before the real
# Platform::Current()->GetGpuFactories() call, which yields null on the host
# and would override the persona answer with false.
#
# This single override is also what makes the supported-value co-derivation
# right: ResolveCallbackIfReady only downgrades supported=false for non-builtin
# codecs (vp9) when powerEfficient=false -- with the persona answer true, vp9
# stays supported like on a real GPU desktop.
#
# Runtime-gated: no APEX_FP_MEDIA_HW_DECODE = stock behavior. Must be emitted
# by the persona layer together with APEX_FP_MEDIA_HW_DECODE (WebCodecs) so
# both APIs agree.
#
# Apply target: third_party/blink/renderer/modules/media_capabilities/
# media_capabilities.cc (anchor edit via scripts/apply_edits.py).
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/media_capabilities/media_capabilities.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/media_capabilities/media_capabilities.cc
@@ MediaCapabilities::GetGpuFactoriesSupport @@
+  // --- apex: persona hw-decode => powerEfficient=true ---
+  if (apex_fp::MediaHwDecode()) {
+    OnGpuFactoriesSupport(callback_id, true, video_codec);
+    return;
+  }
+  // --- end apex ---
   media::GpuVideoAcceleratorFactories* gpu_factories =
       Platform::Current()->GetGpuFactories();
